Cell["\<\
basis is a list of two side vectors. A point is i basis[[1]] + j basis[[2]], \
with i and j running from 0. to 1. in steps 1./m and 1./n.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->2029612268,ExpressionUUID->"189d54e4-1258-f845-af19-f248fbdcdc7a"],

Cell["\<\
Use positive integers m and n. Input patterns allow integers but do not \
explicitly reject zero or negative values.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1806422713,ExpressionUUID->"0183d87e-a2ae-af4e-9ed4-512bb68639a3"],

Cell["\<\
Returns an array of dimensions {m+1,n+2,coordinateDimension}; the first \
sample of each row is appended again to close that loop.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1830236673,ExpressionUUID->"c07f96a8-c8f9-0149-bfb5-5e656845ea6e"],

Cell["\<\
The use of machine-real iteration steps makes the returned coordinates \
numerical.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->937609585,ExpressionUUID->"d491e97e-a258-764d-9ef2-dc1972716177"]
}, Closed]],

